  'food.c6.t':'Adapted to your land','food.c6.d':'Whether you live in Helsinki, Oslo, London or Madrid, your plan uses what your supermarket stocks.',

  'sci.eyebrow':'The evidence','sci.title':'Why it works (and where it is published)',
  'sci.lede':'I invent nothing. I gather published evidence on maximum strength, healthy fats as fuel and the impact of ultra-processed foods. Science applied with judgement, no dogma.',
  'sci.1.t':'Maximum strength and bone density','sci.1.d':'Twelve weeks of squatting at 85–90% of 1RM significantly improved bone mineral density and neuromuscular performance. Heavy load — not speed — is the most effective bone stimulus.',
  'sci.2.t':'Optimal load protocol for bone','sci.2.d':'A 2025 systematic review and meta-analysis establishes that high-intensity training (75–80% 1RM, 3 sessions/week) has the strongest evidence for improving bone density in adults without chronic disease.',
  'sci.3.t':'Strength endurance: the third pillar','sci.3.d':'Concurrent strength and endurance training — when strength is trained first — produces superior neuromuscular adaptations and improves explosive power without sacrificing aerobic capacity.',
  'sci.4.t':'Omega-3: the fat that activates metabolism','sci.4.d':'A 2025 PubMed review documents that EPA and DHA reduce chronic low-grade inflammation, improve insulin sensitivity and protect bone density. Salmon and herring are the densest sources.',
  'sci.5.t':'Fewer carbs, more fat burned','sci.5.d':'A 2025 meta-analysis of randomised controlled trials concludes that low-carbohydrate diets produce greater fat mass loss at equal calories, by shifting the energy substrate towards fatty acids.',
  'sci.6.t':'Healthy fats and bone architecture','sci.6.d':'A 2024 review in Current Osteoporosis Reports establishes that unsaturated fats positively modulate bone metabolism, while saturated fats inhibit it. The Nordic pattern, rich in omega-3, protects the skeleton long-term.',
  'sci.7.t':'Ultra-processed foods: silent inflammation','sci.7.d':'Nature Reviews Immunology (2024) establishes that ultra-processed foods disrupt the balance between the microbiota and immunity, increasing the risk of metabolic syndrome and chronic inflammatory diseases. Eating real food is protection.',
  'sci.8.t':'Nordic pattern and cardiometabolic health','sci.8.d':'A systematic review and meta-analysis published in Diabetologia found consistent reductions in non-HDL cholesterol, fasting insulin, body weight and BMI in people following a Nordic dietary pattern, without caloric restriction.',
  'sci.9.t':'Diet and osteoporosis risk','sci.9.d':'A 2025 meta-analysis concludes that dietary patterns rich in quality protein, omega-3 and vegetables significantly reduce the risk of low bone density, while diets high in ultra-processed foods increase it.',
  'sci.disclaimer':'Notice: Viking Fitness is a training and nutrition education service, not medical treatment. The cited evidence supports the principles of the method; it does not promise individual results. If you have a medical condition, are pregnant or take medication, consult your doctor before starting.',

  'app.eyebrow':'Your saga, recorded','app.title':'The clan app',
  'app.lede':'Everything you do gets written down. Sessions, sets, loads, meals, calories, macros, weight and measurements. The app computes your weekly volume, your trend and your rank within the clan.',
  'app.l1':'Training log with sets, reps and kilos',
  'app.l2':'Food diary with calories and macros, including a Nordic food database',
  'app.l3':'Body weight tracking with a trend chart',
  'app.l4':'Consistency streak and rank progression: from Thrall to Einherjar',
